        "original_id": "6012d741-c41a-5997-9cf8-86c8628d93b6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean-Louis Comolli, André Bazin, Jacques Doniol-Valcroze, Joseph-Marie Lo Duca\n- Organizations: Cahiers du cinéma\n- Works: \"Machines of the Visible\", \"Technique and Ideology: Camera, Perspective, Depth of Field\"\n- Topics: film and media studies\n\nFacts:\n- Cahiers du cinéma is a French film magazine founded in 1951 by André Bazin, Jacques Doniol-Valcroze, and Joseph-Marie Lo Duca.\n- Jean-Louis Comolli was editor in chief of Cahiers du cinéma from 1966 to 1978.\n- Jean-Louis Comolli wrote the influential essay \"Machines of the Visible\" in 1971.\n- Jean-Louis Comolli wrote the influential essay \"Technique and Ideology: Camera, Perspective, Depth of Field\" in 1971 and 1972.\n- Both Jean-Louis Comolli essays were translated in English anthologies of film and media studies.",
